{"type":"message","id":"ae537d4a","parentId":"1343bccd","timestamp":"2026-04-03T07:43:21.624Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, exec is denied. Let me check what's happening - the security policy might be blocking these commands. Let me try a simpler approach and just check if the dashboard is already running somehow, or just try to start it.\n\nActually, looking at the error, it seems exec is being denied due to allowlist misses. This is odd because I should be able to run shell commands. Let me try with different settings or check if there's a specific way to run commands here.\n\nWait, looking at the exec function parameters, there's an `ask` field. Maybe I need to set `ask: \"on-miss\"` or something. Or maybe I need to check the security settings.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the error message: \"exec denied: allowlist miss\" - this suggests there's a security policy in place that requires certain commands to be allowlisted. \n\nLet me try with elevated permissions or check if there's a different way to handle this. But actually, I don't think I can bypass security policies - I should inform the user if there's an issue.\n\nWait, let me re-read the exec tool description. It says \"Exec security mode (deny|allowlist|full)\" and \"Exec ask mode (off|on-miss|always)\". The error says \"allowlist miss\" which means the command isn't in the allowlist.\n\nLet me try to see if I can work around this or need to inform the user. Actually, I should just try running the commands - perhaps the allowlist is populated dynamically or the system handles it differently.\n\nLet me try exec with a very basic command to see if anything works.","thinkingSignature":"c41a3c5304866159395da81c24abfa718d0ccb03d8f934f6f53dbf5d74bfaeaf"},{"type":"text","text":"exec 权限受限，无法直接执行命令来启动 dashboard。让我尝试其他方式：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_bbn5yqfrrn1e_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"echo \"test\"","ask":"on-miss"}}],"api":