{"type":"message","id":"24bf1fe1","parentId":"3b5bd4c1","timestamp":"2026-04-03T07:56:26.296Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dashboard is running and serving HTML correctly. The issue is that the user is getting \"Cannot GET /\" via SSH tunnel. This could be a browser caching issue, or the tunnel isn't correctly set up, or there's something about how the request is being routed.\n\nWait - looking at the curl output, it returns 200 and valid HTML. But the user says they get \"Cannot GET /\". This might be because:\n\n1. The SSH tunnel command they used might be wrong\n2. Browser cache\n3. The page loads via JavaScript and they might be seeing a client-side error\n\nLet me check the actual page content more carefully. Actually the curl output shows it's rendering correctly with \"OpenClaw Bot Dashboard\" title. \n\nBut wait - there's something odd in the HTML output. I see `\"This page could not be found.\"` in the content. Let me look more carefully...\n\nActually looking at the HTML, it seems like the SSR is rendering the page but the client-side routing might have issues. The initial HTML looks fine though.\n\nThe error \"Cannot GET /\" typically comes from Express/Node when a route isn't defined. But this is a Next.js app... unless something is weird with the setup.\n\nLet me check if maybe the issue is that they need to access it differently via the tunnel. When you do `ssh -L 3000:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm`, it should tunnel local port 3000 to remote port 3000. Then accessing `http://localhost:3000` should work.\n\nActually wait - I see in the output there's a 404 page being rendered. The page shows \"思考中...\" (Thinking...) which is a loading state. The issue might be that the client-side JavaScript is trying to fetch data and failing.\n\nActually no, looking at the log output I captured earlier:\n```\n✓ Ready in 1292ms\n○ Compiling / ...\n GET / 200 in 9.8s (compile: 9.4s, render: 419ms)\n\n\n```\n\nThis shows the page was served with 200 status. The \"Cannot GET /\" error the user is seeing might be a timing issue - perhaps they accessed it before compilation finished, or there's a client-side routing problem. Let me check the dashboard logs to see what actually happened when they tried to connect.","thinkingSignature":"0b886d29bbcc328549f7d9825d4a3dea21c2900a4dd7138dee3f8875effb15f0"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_4f5oo88ak9pz_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /tmp/dashboard.log | tail -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":16889,"output":511,"cacheRead":12321,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29721,"cost":{"input":0.0050666999999999995,"output":0.0006131999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0007392599999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00641916}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775202964274,"responseId":"061ea594f91b417846411bab94c75666"}}
