{"type":"message","id":"72535ba8","parentId":"53ee0b0a","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:11:45.183Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dashboard is listening on localhost and 172.18.0.2. The SSH tunnel should work with `ssh -L 3000:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm-0-14-ubuntu`.\n\nLet me think about what could be wrong:\n\n1. The server is accessible at `vm-0-14-ubuntu` (hostname probably resolves to 172.18.0.2 or some other IP)\n2. The user runs `ssh -L 3000:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm-0-14-ubuntu`\n3. This should tunnel local port 3000 to the server's localhost:3000\n\nThe problem could be:\n1. SSH connection fails or doesn't establish\n2. The tunnel is established but browser shows \"Cannot GET /\"\n3. The server's SSH might not allow gatewayports or has AllowTcpForwarding disabled\n\nWait - the user said they get \"Cannot GET /\". That's not a connection refused - that means the tunnel IS working and something IS responding on localhost:3000. But the response is a 404 error page.\n\nActually, looking at the HTML I fetched earlier - it's showing a 404 page. The HTML contains \"404: This page could not be found.\" This means:\n1. The tunnel works (connection succeeds)\n2. Something responds on port 3000\n3. But that something returns 404\n\nThe issue might be that the user's SSH tunnel goes to a different port 3000 on the server - maybe they have another service running on the server's port 3000 that returns 404, while the dashboard is on a different port or path.\n\nOr wait - the `Cannot GET /` error is from Next.js development server. This is actually the dashboard responding, but it shows a 404 because... hmm.\n\nActually, looking at the log, there was `GET / 200` successful requests. So the server IS serving the dashboard correctly. The \"Cannot GET /\" might be from an old session or something else.\n\n\nLet me verify the tunnel is actually working by testing it directly.","thinkingSignature":"e78bc8925f26756f6fd295f292ed2105f53e3718d132a94fbdede740adcabdaf"},{"type":"text","text":"Dashboard 运行正常。让我帮你进一步诊断 SSH 隧道问题：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pzemlmr5c7wb_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ssh -v -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -o ConnectTimeout=5 ubuntu@localhost true 2>&1 | head -20 || echo \"SSH to localhost not available\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pzemlmr5c7wb_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /etc/ssh/sshd_config 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"AllowTcpForwarding|GatewayPorts|ListenAddress\" || echo \"Cannot read sshd_config\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":31154,"output":557,"cacheRead":12321,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":44032,"cost":{"input":0.009346199999999999,"output":0.0006684,"cacheRead":0.0007392599999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010753859999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775203885793,"responseId":"061ea92e9748858a27a81eb56ed99e09"}}
{"type":"message","id":"c6deb8dd","parentId":"72535ba8","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:11:45.300Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_pzemlmr5c7wb_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenSSH_9.2p1 Debian-2+deb12u7, OpenSSL 3.0.18 30 Sep 2025\r\ndebug1: Reading configuration data /etc/ssh/ssh_config\r\ndebug1: /etc/ssh/ssh_config line 19: include /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d/*.conf matched no files\r\ndebug1: /etc/ssh/ssh_config line 21: Applying options for *\r\ndebug1: Connecting to localhost [::1] port 22.\r\ndebug1: connect to address ::1 port 22: Connection refused\r\ndebug1: Connecting to localhost [127.0.0.1] port 22.\r\ndebug1: connect to address 127.0.0.1 port 22: Connection refused\r\nssh: connect to host localhost port 22: Connection refused"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":58,"aggregated":"OpenSSH_9.2p1 Debian-2+deb12u7, OpenSSL 3.0.18 30 Sep 2025\r\ndebug1: Reading configuration data /etc/ssh/ssh_config\r\ndebug1: /etc/ssh/ssh_config line 19: include /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d/*.conf matched no files\r\ndebug1: /etc/ssh/ssh_config line 21: Applying options for *\r\ndebug1: Connecting to localhost [::1] port 22.\r\ndebug1: connect to address ::1 port 22: Connection refused\r\ndebug1: Connecting to localhost [127.0.0.1] port 22.\r\ndebug1: connect to address 127.0.0.1 port 22: Connection refused\r\nssh: connect to host localhost port 22: Connection refused","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775203905281}}
