{"type":"message","id":"5d335143","parentId":"2096c55c","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:15:16.294Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b53c33fddb8a4ee86a29067cef35\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6\",\n  \"sender\": \"听风\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Fri 2026-04-03 08:15 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"听风 (ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6\",\n  \"name\": \"听风\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b53c33fddb8a4ee86a29067cef35]\n听风: % ssh -L 3001:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm-0-14-ubuntu\nWelcome to Ubuntu 20.04 LTS (GNU/Linux 5.4.0-126-generic x86_64)\n\n\n * Documentation:  https://help.ubuntu.com\n * Management:     https://landscape.canonical.com\n * Support:        https://ubuntu.com/advantage\n\n\n  System information as of Fri 03 Apr 2026 04:14:36 PM CST\n\n\n  System load:                      1.46\n  Usage of /:                       65.5% of 88.48GB\n  Memory usage:                     73%\n  Swap usage:                       23%\n  Processes:                        145\n  Users logged in:                  1\n  IPv4 address for br-fa0f4bea722a: 172.18.0.1\n  IPv4 address for docker0:         172.17.0.1\n  IPv4 address for eth0:            10.0.0.14\n  IPv4 address for tailscale0:      100.93.115.18\n  IPv6 address for tailscale0:      fd7a:115c:a1e0::4501:739a\n\n\n  => There are 3 zombie processes.\n\n\n * Ubuntu 20.04 LTS Focal Fossa has reached its end of standard support\n   on 31 May 2025.\n\n\n   For more details see:\n   https://ubuntu.com/20-04\nNew release '22.04.5 LTS' available.\nRun 'do-release-upgrade' to upgrade to it.\n\n\n\n\nLast login: Fri Apr  3 16:12:36 CST 2026 from 100.95.35.113 on pts/1\nubuntu@VM-0-14-ubuntu:~$"}],"timestamp":1775204116278}}
{"type":"message","id":"d433638b","parentId":"5d335143","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:15:27.258Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user has established an SSH tunnel on port 3001 instead of 3000. The tunnel is working (they got a successful SSH login). Now they need to access http://localhost:3001 in their browser.\n\nLooking at the lsof output from before:\n- ssh is listening on localhost:hbci (which is port 3001 - \"hbci\" is the service name for port 3001)\n- ESTABLISHED connection to localhost:54310\n\nSo the tunnel is working! They just need to open http://localhost:3001 in their browser.","thinkingSignature":"aac3aa853bd8a60d151e2fe85685b7d5ab097e47413b5f190345e741bc60b836"},{"type":"text","text":"SSH 隧道已经建立成功了！ 🎉\n\n你映射的是 **3001 → 3000**，所以访问地址应该是：\n\n**http://localhost:3001**\n\n在浏览器直接打开这个地址就可以了。\n\n如果不行，试试用浏览器隐身模式打开。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":39,"output":173,"cacheRead":44742,"cacheWrite":242,"totalTokens":45196,"cost":{"input":0.0000117,"output":0.00020759999999999998,"cacheRead":0.0026845199999999997,"cacheWrite":0.00009075,"total":0.00299457}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775204116291,"responseId":"061eaa14bbf0fd10c4c8dd154bef828a"}}
{"type":"message","id":"c5b7243a","parentId":"d433638b","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:16:38.866Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b53c338f2c4a4ee7e12822eff223\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6\",\n  \"sender\": \"听风\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Fri 2026-04-03 08:16 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"听风 (ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6\",\n  \"name\": \"听风\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b53c338f2c4a4ee7e12822eff223]\n听风: 还是打开只有 Cannot GET /"}],"timestamp":1775204198847}}
{"type":"message","id":"c75c3d2b","parentId":"c5b7243a","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:17:10.755Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is still getting \"Cannot GET /\" when accessing via the SSH tunnel. The issue is likely that the Next.js app is listening on localhost inside the container/VM, but when accessed via SSH port forwarding from outside, the connection is going to the wrong place.\n\nLet me think about the network topology:\n1. The user's local machine: localhost:3001 -> SSH tunnel -> VM's SSH server -> forwards to localhost:3000 on VM\n2. The Next.js app on the VM is listening on localhost:3000 and 172.18.0.2:3000\n\nWhen the user does `ssh -L 3001:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm-0-14-ubuntu`, the `localhost` in `localhost:3000` refers to the VM's localhost, not the user's localhost. So the tunnel should correctly forward to the VM's localhost:3000 where Next.js is listening.\n\nBut wait - looking at the lsof output from the server earlier, it showed the Next.js app is running. Let me think about what's happening.\n\nThe issue could be that:\n1. The Next.js app is listening inside a Docker container where localhost is different from the VM's localhost\n2. The app is actually listening on a specific interface, not on all interfaces including localhost\n\nWait, looking at the Next.js log again:\n```\n- Local:         http://localhost:3000\n- Network:       http://172.18.0.2:3000\n```\n\nThis suggests it IS listening on localhost:3000.\n\nBut wait - the lsof output I ran earlier was on the server. The user is saying that from their local machine via the SSH tunnel, they get \"Cannot GET /\". But the server shows everything is working.\n\nActually, I think I might understand. The user's SSH command is:\n`ssh -L 3001:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm-0-14-ubuntu`\n\n\nWhen the SSH tunnel connects to `localhost:3000` on the VM, it's hitting the VM's port 3000 where Next.js is bound. The \"Cannot GET /\" response suggests something is responding, but maybe there's another service running on the VM's localhost:3000 that's not the Next.js app, or there's a routing issue within the container/VM network. The curl test from the server worked fine, so the app itself is functional - the problem seems to be with how the SSH tunnel is routing to it.\n\nActually, I should reconsider the network topology. The server is a containerized environment (indicated by docker0 at 172.17.0.1 and the existence of a Docker init process). The Node.js app is running directly on the host inside this container environment. When the user establishes an SSH tunnel with `ssh -L 3001:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm-0-14-ubuntu`, they're forwarding their local port 3001 to the remote server's localhost:3000. The issue might be that the SSH connection is working, but the service responding on the remote end isn't the Next.js app - it could be something else running on that port, or there's a mismatch between what the user expects and what's actually running.","thinkingSignature":"574bdd7182968921b47313cb4b5fb7b6197a10f3e9d4f0b56db75808506e6675"},{"type":"text","text":"\n让我检查一下服务器端的状态：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_knms5ao3184a_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s http://localhost:3000 | head -10"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":39,"output":702,"cacheRead":44742,"cacheWrite":508,"totalTokens":45991,"cost":{"input":0.0000117,"output":0.0008424,"cacheRead":0.0026845199999999997,"cacheWrite":0.0001905,"total":0.00372912}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775204198863,"responseId":"061eaa675947c619b440350e243bcd08"}}
