{"type":"message","id":"afad807f","parentId":"b75d68f4","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:17:57.230Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"服务器上 curl 返回 200 和完整 HTML。但关键是，页面内容显示的是 `<p class=\"text-[var(--text-muted)]\">思考中...</p>` - 这是 SSR 的初始加载状态，说明页面加载时在等待 JavaScript 水合（hydration）。\n\n问题可能是：\n1. Next.js 开发模式下，页面需要编译，首次加载会比较慢\n2. SSH 隧道虽然通了，但网络延迟导致页面加载不完整\n3. 用户看到的 \"Cannot GET /\" 可能是浏览器显示的错误，但实际响应可能是 200\n\n让我建议用户：\n1. 在本地 Mac 上用 curl 测试一下隧道是否真的通\n2. 等待更长时间让 Next.js 编译完成\n3. 清除浏览器缓存\n\n实际上，我应该让用户在本地 Mac 上运行一个 curl 命令来测试 tunnel 是否真的工作。但我现在无法直接控制用户的机器，只能让用户自己运行命令。\n\n让我告诉用户这个情况。","thinkingSignature":"631cd5288db3c9d02b63eace078f5a0054d304de521c7baaeb7f917a65598346"},{"type":"text","text":"服务器上 curl 测试完全正常，返回 200 和完整的 Dashboard HTML。\n\n问题可能是：\n\n1. **Next.js 开发模式首次加载需要编译** — 等待 10-20 秒让 JS 完全加载\n2. **浏览器显示的是旧的缓存** — 需要强制刷新\n\n**请在你的 Mac 上运行这个命令测试隧道是否真的通：**\n\n```bash\ncurl -s http://localhost:3001 | head -5\n```\n\n如果返回 HTML，说明隧道通了，只是浏览器需要刷新/等待。如果返回 \"Connection refused\" 或空白，说明隧道没建立成功。\n\n另外，你的 SSH 终端窗口必须**保持开着**，隧道是在 SSH 会话期间建立的。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":57610,"output":324,"cacheRead":12321,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":70255,"cost":{"input":0.017283,"output":0.00038879999999999996,"cacheRead":0.0007392599999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01841106}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775204260750,"responseId":"061eaaa5715d8f81bf9202010ea55199"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a9f1e680","parentId":"afad807f","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:23:51.959Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b53c3df8d94a0ee7ad7d7e3c7c50\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6\",\n  \"sender\": \"听风\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Fri 2026-04-03 08:23 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"听风 (ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_8d379606db2e0a64b8dbda39b4671fa6\",\n  \"name\": \"听风\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b53c3df8d94a0ee7ad7d7e3c7c50]\n听风:  % curl -s http://localhost:3001          \n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Error</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<pre>Cannot GET /</pre>\n</body>\n</html>\n\n\n还是说明没东西啊"}],"timestamp":1775204631941}}
{"type":"message","id":"f1068808","parentId":"a9f1e680","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:24:20.576Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the user is getting `Cannot GET /` when curling localhost:3001. But on the server, curling localhost:3000 returns proper HTML.\n\nThis is strange. Let me think about what could cause this...\n\nWait - looking at the error \"Cannot GET /\" - this is actually a response from something. The HTML format with `<pre>Cannot GET /</pre>` looks like an Express.js or similar error, not the Next.js app's error page.\n\nThe issue might be:\n1. There's a process on the server that IS listening on port 3000 but it's NOT the Next.js dashboard\n2. Or there's a proxy/container setup that's routing traffic incorrectly\n\nActually wait - I tested from the server and got proper HTML. But the user tunneling to the same port gets \"Cannot GET /\". This suggests maybe:\n\n1. The server has multiple network interfaces and the service is bound to localhost only, but SSH tunnel connects via a different interface\n2. There's another service already using port 3000 that the tunnel connects to instead of the Next.js app\n\nLet me check - the Next.js dev server says it's listening on \"localhost:3000\" and \"172.18.0.2:3000\". So it should be accessible via both.\n\nBut wait - the user's tunnel command is:\n`ssh -L 3001:localhost:3000 ubuntu@vm-0-14-ubuntu`\n\nThis means: forward local 3001 to remote localhost:3000. So when the user accesses localhost:3001, it should tunnel to the server's localhost:3000.\n\nIf curl on the server returns proper content for localhost:3000 but curl via the tunnel returns \"Cannot GET /\", something is wrong with the routing.\n\nActually wait - could there be a previous/unrelated process that was set up by the user previously that is still running and listening on port 3000? The \"Cannot GET /\" with that specific HTML format looks like it could be from a different application.\n\n\nThe Next.js dashboard I started is definitely running based on the process list and logs. But maybe the user's previous attempt left something else running on port 3000 that's now intercepting the tunnel traffic instead.\n\nSince the tunnel command maps remote localhost:3000 to local 3001, the issue might be that an older process on the server is still bound to 3000 and handling the requests differently than the current Next.js instance. I should suggest killing any stale processes and restarting fresh.","thinkingSignature":"078cc8cff72e19e79df29a27c053120829a9c12b7bbe6ffb4cb8fa8bee0cbb4d"},{"type":"text","text":"这就是问题所在！服务器上 `localhost:3000` 实际上有别的东西在响应（不是你刚才启动的 Dashboard）。\n\n让我检查一下服务器上 3000 端口到底是什么在服务：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_yfupy3coehmn_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -v http://localhost:3000 2>&1 | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":39,"output":588,"cacheRead":3779,"cacheWrite":65245,"totalTokens":69651,"cost":{"input":0.0000117,"output":0.0007056,"cacheRead":0.00022674,"cacheWrite":0.024466875,"total":0.025410915}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775204631956,"responseId":"061eac18f49a90a20f59f6e09ee3c74c"}}
