{"type":"message","id":"00399c21","parentId":"5b030893","timestamp":"2026-04-03T08:41:29.013Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking where the non-standard whitespace characters came from - was it the OpenClaw source code or somewhere else that wrote the config file.\n\nLooking at the problem:\n- The `\\u00a0` (non-breaking space) characters were found in the `openclaw.json` config file\n- These characters were embedded in the JSON structure, specifically after `\"agentToAgent\": {`\n\nThe source of these characters could be:\n1. The OpenClaw config writing code itself (if it wrote these chars accidentally)\n2. Some editor or process that modified the file\n3. The wizard/doctor command that last touched the file (based on the meta data showing \"lastRunCommand\": \"doctor\")\n\nLooking at the \"meta\" section:\n```json\n\"meta\": {\n    \"lastTouchedVersion\": \"2026.4.1\",\n    \"lastTouchedAt\": \"2026-04-02T12:48:31.896Z\"\n  },\n  \"wizard\": {\n    \"lastRunAt\": \"2026-04-02T12:48:31.861Z\",\n    \"lastRunVersion\": \"2026.4.1\",\n    \"lastRunCommand\": \"doctor\",\n    \"lastRunMode\": \"local\"\n  }\n```\n\nSo the file was last touched by the \"doctor\" command on April 2, 2026. The doctor command likely wrote the config file.\n\nThe issue is probably in OpenClaw's own code that writes the config - it probably used some string formatting that accidentally inserted non-breaking spaces, or there's a bug in how it generates the JSON.\n\nBut I shouldn't speculate too much - I should just answer that it was likely OpenClaw's own code that wrote these characters, since the file was last touched by OpenClaw itself (doctor command).","thinkingSignature":"1b76a611bb913ea646270a1988b526cb652f5377a2e959edf6d9da24c631e548"},{"type":"text","text":"看起来是 **OpenClaw 自己的代码问题**。\n\n从文件 metadata 看，`openclaw.json` 最后一次被修改是在 2026-04-02，运行的是 `doctor` 命令。说明是 OpenClaw 在更新配置时写入了这些非标准空白字符。\n\n可能是 OpenClaw 的配置写入代码里用了某种字符串拼接，意外混入了 `